#: ../../source/hermes-gateway-troubleshooting_SKILL.md:27
msgid ""
"Problem: Telegram \"401\" or \"Another gateway is already using this "
"token\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hermes-gateway-troubleshooting_SKILL.md:29
msgid ""
"This is **NOT** an authentication failure. The token is valid. It's a "
"**scoped lock conflict** between multiple gateway instances using the "
"same bot token."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hermes-gateway-troubleshooting_SKILL.md:31
msgid "Root Causes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hermes-gateway-troubleshooting_SKILL.md:33
msgid ""
"**Scoped lock conflict** — Hermes uses file-based locks to prevent "
"multiple gateways from polling the same Telegram bot simultaneously."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hermes-gateway-troubleshooting_SKILL.md:34
msgid ""
"**Env var override** — `TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN` set in env (systemd "
"`.service` file, `gateway.env`, or `~/.env`) **overrides** `enabled: "
"false` in `config.yaml`. The gateway reads the env var and connects "
"regardless of the config setting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hermes-gateway-troubleshooting_SKILL.md:35
msgid ""
"**Systemd service file** — The `/etc/systemd/system/hermes-"
"gateway.service` may hardcode `Environment=TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=...`. This "
"takes priority over ALL config.yaml settings. You MUST remove it from the"
" service file if you want to disable Telegram on the default agent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hermes-gateway-troubleshooting_SKILL.md:36
msgid ""
"**Per-session gateway spawning** — Each new CLI session can spawn its own"
" gateway process, which conflicts with systemd-managed gateways."
msgstr ""

